const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can I see the Great Migration year-round in the Serengeti?', a: 'The wildebeest are in the Serengeti ecosystem for about 8 to 9 months of the year. The dramatic river crossings only happen when the herds are in the north (Mara River, June to October). Outside this window you can still see large groups of wildebeest elsewhere in the Serengeti, particularly during calving season (January to February) in the south.' },
